 &nbsp; 
 
 
 Final Numbers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep ; Chart: Dan Primack/Axios GE is back in the mega-takeover game , this morning agreeing to buy Consolidated Precision Products for $11.75 billion from Warburg Pincus and Berkshire Partners.

 This is CEO Larry Culp's largest acquisition in his eight years at the helm. Cleveland-based CPP is a major supplier of airfoil castings, a critical component in airplane engines at a time when airplane engines are in high demand. 
 
